# Keep the Cloud Build upload small: never ship build output, VCS, or local envs.
.git/
target/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv*/
**/.venv*/
sdk/**/dist/
sdk/**/native/
*.log

# CREDENTIAL EXCLUSIONS — the twin of the block in .dockerignore, stated separately
# because the two lists govern different transfers. gcloud uses THIS file INSTEAD of
# .gitignore when it exists, so a gitignored path is not excluded unless it is named
# here; and `gcloud builds submit ... .` uploads the whole context to
# gs://<project>_cloudbuild/source/*.tgz, readable by every principal with
# project-level storage read and retained after the build. .dockerignore keeps a file
# out of an image LAYER only — it does not keep it out of that tarball.
#
# `work/` is where the runbooks and the `scripts/test-*-cloud.sh.example` headers tell
# an operator to keep FILLED-IN cloud credential scripts, precisely because it is
# gitignored. That also makes `tracked_secrets_gate.py` blind to it by construction:
# that gate scans TRACKED files. On this path the ignore list is the only control.
work/
**/work/
# Local agent and editor state. Gitignored, so this list is again the only control:
# `.claude/settings.local.json` is where env vars and MCP server tokens live, and the
# skill tree next to it holds private review material.
.claude/
**/.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.verification/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*-seed
**/*seed.txt
**/kubeconfig
.aws/
.gcloud/
.kube/
